tely from home (from point 6). Therefore, James must have lunch at home (from point 4). This scenario also satisfies the statement.\n\n4. If James is not a manager and does not appear in the company today, then he cannot have lunch in the company (from point 2). Since he is not a manager, he cannot work remotely from home (from point 6). Therefore, James must have lunch at home (from point 4). This scenario also satisfies the statement.\n\nSince all scenarios satisfy the statement, the statement is true.\n\n# Answer:\n\\The correct option is: A",
